    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7973567b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: starving_mexican_monkey_eating_peanuts; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a monkey perched on a bare tree, with the overlaid text 'starving mexican monkey eating peanuts.' This juxtaposition maps the visual of a monkey (a primate) onto a human group (Mexicans), using the monkey as a dehumanizing and derogatory metaphor. The text implies that Mexicans are 'starving' and 'eating peanuts,' which is a grotesque and false stereotype. This is a clear example of anti-Latino/hispanic racism, as it uses a primate metaphor to demean and dehumanize a specific ethnic group, fitting the 'Comparing Black people to primates' and 'Anti-Latino/Hispanic Stereotypes' categories from the provided knowledge base. The intent is to portray Mexicans as primitive, impoverished, and inferior, which is a hateful and harmful message targeting a specific community based on ethnicity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_014dc5be"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
